From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: keep firstInstance on gpu_prerast CPU instance splits
 biblioklept

gpu_prerast_split() and gpu_prerast_split_fan() cut a draw over the
prerast arena on the CPU: by instance ranges when one instance fits,
else per instance into vertex windows. Each chunk was drawn with
instance.base = firstInstance + its first instance. The lowered VS adds
gl_BaseInstance (the vs.base_instance sysval) to its instance ID for
gl_InstanceIndex, and the attribute descriptors add base * stride to
per-instance attributes, so gl_InstanceIndex stayed right but every
chunk saw gl_BaseInstance = firstInstance + offset, and an
instance-rate attribute with divisor d read element
firstInstance + offset + i / d instead of firstInstance +
(offset + i) / d (divisor 0 read element firstInstance + offset).

The GPU chunk loop already does this right: it keeps the API
firstInstance in the chunk record and hands the chunk start to the
lowered VS as params.chunk_instance, which the VS adds to
load_instance_id (the ID the attribute fetch and gl_InstanceIndex use).
Do the same for the CPU splits: the chunks keep instance.base, and
gpu_prerast_draw_split() sets cmdbuf->state.gpu_prerast_inst_base to
the chunk's instance offset around its panvk_cmd_draw(). gpu_prerast_vs()
stores it as chunk_instance for a direct lowering, or adds it to the
planner's chunk_instance when the chunk goes through the GPU chunk loop
(an instance range over the 2048 instance cap). Nested splits add up.
The value is CS-builder state only, not a struct panvk_draw_info field,
so the shared panvk_cmd_draw.h (which jm-v9 patches) is not touched.

A chunk that is not lowered after all (IDVS fallback of a VS with
side effects whose lowered variants are missing) has no instance ID
offset: panvk_cmd_draw() folds the offset back into instance.base
there, which is the old behaviour. gpu_prerast_lowers() is the
lowering decision gpu_prerast_draw() already made, factored out so the
fold uses the same test.

Generated draws (the raster passthrough of the arena) never read the
offset; their records are indexed by the compute invocation IDs.

Not changed: indexed triangle fans with primitive restart over the
arena and indirect triangle fans over the arena are still
gpu_prerast_unhandled (see worklogs/driver-remaining/
191-base-instance-splits.md for the plan).

PanProbe large_draw gains base_inst_* cases that capture
gl_BaseInstance and a per-instance attribute (divisor 3 when
vertexAttributeInstanceRateDivisor is exposed) across instance splits,
per-instance vertex windows and fan splits.

Build-only; not device-tested.

